Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: deliver EAPOL exception frames to the host

NSS 12.5 sends EAPOL frames to the host as a special-data exception of
type NSS_WIFI_VDEV_EXT_DATA_PKT_TYPE_EAPOL. Without a case for it the
frame reaches the default branch and is dropped, so a client cannot finish
the 4-way handshake. Deliver it through ath11k_nss_deliver_rx like other
received frames. The enum does not exist in the 11.4 headers, so the case
is compiled out when CONFIG_NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_11_4 is set.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -896,6 +896,12 @@ ath11k_nss_vdev_special_data_receive(str
 		dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
 #endif
 	break;
+#ifndef CONFIG_NSS_FIRMWARE_VERSION_11_4
+	case NSS_WIFI_VDEV_EXT_DATA_PKT_TYPE_EAPOL:
+		/* Without this case the frame reaches the default branch and is dropped. */
+		ath11k_nss_deliver_rx(arvif->vif, skb, eth_decap, data_offs, napi);
+	break;
+#endif
 	default:
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "unsupported pkt_type %d from nss\n", wifi_metadata->pkt_type);
 		dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
